# Syllogism: a missing premise
# Can a universal implication alone establish its particular conclusion?

# This source is expected not to pass. Inspect the red source-local feedback.
# Add $is_human(socrates) at the start of the outer forall body, then check.
abstract_prop is_human(person)
abstract_prop is_mortal(person)

forall people nonempty_set, socrates people:
    forall person people:
        $is_human(person)
        =>:
            $is_mortal(person)
    =>:
        # Not proving mortality does not prove immortality.
        # Compare the two premises with the passing syllogism lesson.
        $is_mortal(socrates)
